flowchart TB
  accTitle: Product X payment-timeout recovery contract
  accDescr: In the illustrative Product X case, a payment request times out and settlement is unknown. The parent task and no-duplicate-charge invariant are preserved. A bounded child scope performs read-only status checks using the original transaction and idempotency reference. It returns settled, not-settled, or still-unknown with evidence. The parent validates the result and current version before acting. A narrowly guarded rule may later be tested only after repeated validated episodes.
  A[Payment attempt times out] --> B[Classify: outcome unknown]
  B --> C[Preserve parent version and no-duplicate-charge invariant]
  C --> D[Open child: read-only status check]
  D --> E{Provider evidence}
  E -->|settled| F[Return SETTLED]
  E -->|not settled| G[Return NOT_SETTLED]
  E -->|no reliable status| H[Return STILL_UNKNOWN]
  F --> V[Validate parent version, evidence and dependencies]
  G --> V
  H --> V
  V --> P[Parent resumes, retries under policy, or escalates]
  V --> Q[Validated trace may become guarded rule candidate]
  classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E
  classDef process fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E
